    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line on successful owner creation, via the logger named `AUDIT`, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\nI added the audit logging to the final step of the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`) \u2014 the \"on successful create\" responder, which runs after the owner has been saved and has all three values populated:\n\n- Declared a logger `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` (slf4j, consistent with existing logger usage in the codebase).\n- Logged `Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}` with `owner.getId()`, `owner.getCustomerCode()`, and `owner.getRegistrationDate()` before sending the 201 response.\n\nThe `registrationDate` is logged via `LocalDate.toString()`, which produces ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 matching the DTO's `format: date` serialization, so the test's substring assertion against the fetched owner's JSON `registrationDate` holds.\n\nResults: the new `Cp21Tests.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes, and the full suite is green (32 tests, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
